# Requirements that are marked Complete and are excluded from the important-gates must-be-covered
# set (plan 09-05, EV-04, amendment A-01). The must-be-covered set is derived from the requirement
# records under .planning/; this file is the only thing subtracted from it.
# One line per exclusion: '<REQ> <reason>', the reason being words joined by underscores (at least
# three) that name the evidence the requirement actually has. There are two categories: a close
# record or release action instead of a gate mechanism, and gate-machinery self-evidence (a step,
# the local gate command, a suite test id, or the registration commit itself).
# The toy tree needs none of them: its two requirement records list exactly the ids the toy registry
# covers and mark every one of them Complete, so the derived set and the registry agree by
# construction.
#allow-empty: the toy registry covers every requirement its records mark Complete
EV-99 not_a_gate_mechanism_at_all
